<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammed Dib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–2003</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammed Dib (1920–2003) was an Algerian novelist and poet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a>, writing in French. His trilogy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, beginning with La Grande Maison (1952), portrayed poverty and growing political awareness among Algerians under colonial rule. Expelled from Algeria in 1959, he lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> for the rest of his life and continued to publish novels and poetry.</p></div>
